    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d402">

                <pb facs="0494" n="382" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg382"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/138: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-19T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1919,
                                6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2346. For the Secretary of State.</p>
                <p>Referring to Department’s 2315, June 16, 4 p.m.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d402-f1"/>
                    Mr. Znamensky, who states he is Assistant Minister of Food and Supplies for the
                    Russian Government at Omsk, desires to purchase uniforms and overcoats or cloth
                    for manufacture thereof; underwear, stockings, shoes, caps, et cetera;
                    machinery, tools, rations, motor vehicles and other supplies, excepting
                    munitions of war.</p>
                <p>Russian Embassy here inform me his credentials authentic. He proposes payment
                    upon credit basis or by a loan or such other method of payment and security as
                    may prove acceptable.</p>
                <p>What attitude is Department to assume? …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
